+## Imports
+
+`POST /import/items` and `POST /import/sales` take `{ "csv": "..." }`. A file
+is imported whole or not at all; the error message names the row (`row 2` is
+the first data row). `POST /import/sales` (columns `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`)
+answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }`: the tickets imported and the dishes
+sold on them (the sum of `qty`); tickets imported before are skipped and not
+counted. An item running out answers `not_enough_stock_row` (409).
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers one line per
+item with use in those days: `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual,
+difference }`.
