+## Sales
+
+- A sale is one line of a till ticket: `ticket`, `soldAt` (instant), `dishId`,
+  `qty` (whole dishes) and `use`, the ingredient quantities it stood for when
+  it was imported (one recipe portion per dish). Its stock is consumed at
+  `soldAt` with the ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>`.
+- A ticket is imported once; importing it again does nothing. A file is
+  imported whole or not at all. `sales` may be missing in older files (no
+  sales yet).
+- Variance compares, per item and over UTC days, the theoretical use (the
+  `use` of sales sold in those days) with the actual use (every `consume`
+  movement in those days); the difference is actual minus theoretical.
